options.description:
Whether to enable https://github.com/microsoft/azure-pipelines-language-server An Azure
Pipelines language server `azure-pipelines-ls` can be installed via
`npm`:

``` sh
npm install -g azure-pipelines-language-server
```

By default `azure-pipelines-ls` will only work in files named
`azure-pipelines.yml`, this can be changed by providing additional
settings like so:

``` lua
vim.lsp.config('azure_pipelines_ls', {
  ... -- other configuration
  settings = {
      yaml = {
          schemas = {
              ["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/microsoft/azure-pipelines-vscode/master/service-schema.json"] = {
                  "/azure-pipeline*.y*l",
                  "/*.azure*",
                  "Azure-Pipelines/**/*.y*l",
                  "Pipelines/*.y*l",
              },
          },
      },
  },
})
```

The Azure Pipelines LSP is a fork of `yaml-language-server` and as such
the same settings can be passed to it as `yaml-language-server`..

